        "Attributes": [
          {
            "Id": 758301,
            "attributeType": "LongString",
            "attributeName": "AIDescription",
            "attributeRelationType": "None",
            "Value": "The Nintendo 64 (N64) was a revolutionary home video game console released by Nintendo in 1996, marking their third major console and a key player in the fifth generation of gaming. Featuring a 64-bit CPU and a unique coprocessor for graphics and sound, it introduced the thumbstick controller and supported multiplayer with four controller ports. While commercially successful in North America, it faced challenges in Japan and Europe, partly due to its reliance on ROM cartridges instead of optical discs.\n\nDespite a smaller library of 388 games compared to its competitors, the N64 delivered groundbreaking experiences like *Super Mario 64*, *GoldenEye 007*, and *The Legend of Zelda: Ocarina of Time*, which are considered among the greatest games ever made. Its innovations in 3D graphics and gameplay continue to influence game design today, and it remains an iconic console in video game history."
          },
